                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "892c5552-ebbb-311a-ac80-59f385aa8b4d",
                        "entry_id": "5e8c5c55-cd7a-35d3-a823-63fa1ec4500b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "физ. безмассовая элементарная частица, переносчик сильного взаимодействия"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "befbfeb2-97a8-4123-a4c1-1414b18a25d0",
                                "sense_id": "892c5552-ebbb-311a-ac80-59f385aa8b4d",
                                "text": "Как и кварки, глюоны являются цветными частицами, но поскольку каждый глюон изменяет цвета сразу двух кварков (кварка, который испускает глюон, и кварка, который поглотил глюон), то глюон окрашен дважды, неся на себе цвет и антицвет, как правило, отличный от цвета."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6288e184-524f-4347-99ad-c1a0124491eb",
                        "source_entry_id": "5e8c5c55-cd7a-35d3-a823-63fa1ec4500b",
                        "source_sense_id": "892c5552-ebbb-311a-ac80-59f385aa8b4d",
                        "source_sense_description": "элементарная частица",
                        "target_lang_word": "gluon",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "gluon",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "030acf5b-598c-346b-a728-21e7642936cf",
                                        "entry_id": "39fcc0d9-1447-391a-b621-627001569d64",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A massless gauge boson that binds quarks together to form baryons, mesons and other hadrons and is associated with the strong nuclear force."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "particle"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bbda9314-5d87-4309-a531-591f0016cdcb",
                                                "sense_id": "030acf5b-598c-346b-a728-21e7642936cf",
                                                "text": "Naive realism might ask today: Tell me what space is in itself, not in terms of other things. Tell me what a gluon is at bottom, or a neutrino, or a charge."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2279cf6a-dfd2-4da5-a49a-f7fcd39a08c7",
                                                "sense_id": "030acf5b-598c-346b-a728-21e7642936cf",
                                                "text": "The so-called spin crisis has had important effects beyond simply confronting theorists with a particularly sharp challenge to their incomplete understanding of quantum chromodynamics, the underlying field theory of quarks and the gluons that mediate their strong interactions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b52df889-7e48-48e4-a02f-ca176870218d",
                                                "sense_id": "030acf5b-598c-346b-a728-21e7642936cf",
                                                "text": "Lattice QCD explores the particle realm by taking a different tack. It simulates quark and gluon behaviors by applying the full QCD theory to a tiny grid like facsimile of the space-time in which particles actually interact."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "72b74539-1749-409a-8803-d0db3d3be4cc",
                        "source_entry_id": "5e8c5c55-cd7a-35d3-a823-63fa1ec4500b",
                        "source_sense_id": "892c5552-ebbb-311a-ac80-59f385aa8b4d",
                        "source_sense_description": "элементарная частица",
                        "target_lang_word": "gluón",
                        "target_lang_code": "es",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "gluón",
                                "target_lang_code": "es",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fc03ea94-f115-3bb1-becf-eacbb44fe84e",
                                        "entry_id": "745843d1-37c1-37ca-96fb-bcb56939b233",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Partícula subatómica, del tipo bosón, que mantiene a los quarks unidos en la conformación de otras partículas como los neutrones. No tiene masa ni carga eléctrica, pero sí carga de color, por lo que puede tanto transmitir como experimentar el tipo de fuerza entre partículas conocida como interacción nuclear fuerte."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
